{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"A key inefficiency is now clear: the current grid assigns one head per program, so short sequences execute mostly padded matrix rows and reload shared KV up to 16 times. I’m adding a head-flattened tile that packs all 16 heads of each token together; it preserves semantics while making the short-prefix and many-sequence cases much denser."}}
